`--output json` prints exactly one JSON object carrying the operation's result fields, and
nothing else on stdout. The flag is accepted after the verb as well as before it.

-- cmd --
booping-tracker comment --issue LIN-1 --body hi --output json
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
{"receipt": "comment LIN-1: cli driver, no-op", "target": "LIN-1", "url": null, "verb": "comment"}
-- stderr --
